{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "8e6ed99c-a3e0-42c0-9f81-a89b1e340757"/*Sketch*/,
  "Description": "Draws freehand sketches over the output as annotations or storyboards.\n\nSketches are stored in pages that are bound to the time at which they were drawn, so a storyboard or frame-by-frame animation can be created by drawing at different times. Strokes are saved automatically to a file.\n\nWhile the operator is selected and the mouse is over the output window, it takes over the keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl shortcuts like undo keep working):\n- B: brush mode (Shift+drag continues the last stroke as a straight line)\n- F: fill mode, each stroke becomes a filled shape in the stroke color\n- E: erase mode, also erases the selection\n- S: lasso select (Shift adds to the selection), Esc clears it\n- G / R: move / scale the selection, click or Enter applies, Esc cancels\n- C: copy the selection, or the whole page if nothing is selected\n- X: cut the selection, or the whole page\n- V: paste and select the copied strokes, also onto an empty frame or into another sketch\n- 1-9: select brush size, [ / ] make it smaller / larger (ß / ´ on German keyboards), Ctrl+drag resizes it (right or up grows)\n- Q: color square around the current color: horizontal is opacity, vertical is brightness, Shift with horizontal movement changes the hue. Click or Q applies, Esc cancels; hold Q, move and release to apply in one go. With a selection it recolors the selection, otherwise it sets the stroke color.\n\nChanging the stroke color while strokes are selected recolors them. All edits can be undone with Ctrl+Z.\n\nAKA: draw, paint, annotate, storyboard, doodle",
  "SymbolTags": "64",
